{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116422","id":3296245892,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7EeLiE","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116422","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116422.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116422.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116422","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116422/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116422/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116422/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b8f7bdf358b9428cbb66692e1ead0e1205c3a6dd","number":116422,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Core: Add non-finite checks to Transform3D::interpolate_with() and Basis::get_quaternion()","user":{"login":"miguelrsgoncalves","id":199957095,"node_id":"U_kgDOC-saZw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199957095?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelrsgoncalves","html_url":"https://github.com/miguelrsgoncalves","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelrsgoncalves/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelrsgoncalves/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelrsgoncalves/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelrsgoncalves/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelrsgoncalves/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelrsgoncalves/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelrsgoncalves/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelrsgoncalves/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelrsgoncalves/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Summary of changes\r\nAdded `is_finite()` checks to `Transform3D::interpolate_with()` and `Basis::get_quaternion()` to provide clearer error reporting for non-finite values (NaN/INF).\r\n\r\n### Motivation\r\nFixes #73299. The current error message \"Basis must be normalized in order to be casted to a Quaternion\" confused developers on what the actual cause is for the error in cases where the transforms or weight were not finite. This change helps developers identify the root cause faster.\r\n\r\n### Technical overview\r\n* **Transform3D**: Added checks for the starting transform, destination transform, and interpolation weight. This ensures the function fails early with a specific message before performing math with NaN or INF values.\r\n* **Basis**: Added a check to `get_quaternion()` to catch non-finite bases. This prevents the code from reaching the `is_rotation()` check, which was the source of the confusing \"not normalized\" error reported in the issue.\r\n\r\n### Testing\r\nTested using the reproduction script provided in issue #73299.\r\n\r\n**Result:** The console now provides a stack trace specific to the non-finite values, rather than a generic normalization error.\r\n\r\n```text\r\nE 0:00:00:886   character_body_3d.gd:27 @ _ready(): The starting transform is not finite, contains NaN or INF.\r\n  <C++ Error>   Condition \"!is_finite()\" is true. Returning: Transform3D()\r\n  <C++ Source>  core\\math\\transform_3d.cpp:98 @ Transform3D::interpolate_with()\r\n  <Stack Trace> character_body_3d.gd:27 @ _ready()\r\n\r\nE 0:00:00:893   Basis::get_quaternion: The Basis is not finite, contains NaN or INF.\r\n  <C++ Error>   Condition \"!is_finite()\" is true. Returning: Quaternion()\r\n  <C++ Source>  core\\math\\basis.cpp:716 @ Basis::get_quaternion()","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"en